    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I never studied math beyond high school, and my vocational diploma didn’t include advanced math. I find it practical when it comes to everyday life, like budgeting or understanding data in games or apps. I don’t see it as a subject I’m deeply connected to, but I appreciate how it underpins technology and design—especially in computer science, which I enjoy.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. I’ve never felt overwhelmed by math problems, even if I didn’t study them deeply. My anxiety comes from not knowing the subject, not from the math itself. I’ve learned to accept that I don’t need to be an expert—just able to understand basics when needed. I’m more comfortable with logic and patterns than with complex equations.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I used AI tools like chatbots to explain basic concepts, especially when learning about functions or graphs. I found them helpful for quick clarifications, like how to plot a parabola. The experience was positive—simple, fast, and non-judgmental. I didn’t use AI for deep learning, but it helped me feel less lost when I needed a quick explanation.",
